        "rephrase": {},
        "profile": "AI engineer (MSc Data Science, University of Bristol) who builds the harness around the model: at AstraZeneca, built a tool-calling agent (LangChain, Claude Haiku 4.5 on AWS Bedrock) that recovers when its tools fail (circuit breakers with a 19,213-gene parquet fallback, deterministic Ensembl and HGNC calls) and diagnosed its failures layer by layer with a three-tier, ~65-test evaluation harness, which also validated a Groq-to-Bedrock model migration. Owns data workflows end-to-end in Python and SQL, from merging structured, API and web-scraped data through feature creation, tuning, validation and deployment (Docker, GitHub Actions CI/CD, MLflow, AWS Lambda). Production LLM agent work on an AstraZeneca-affiliated multi-omics research platform."
      },
