    "profile": "AI engineer (MSc Data Science, University of Bristol) who builds the harness around the model: at AstraZeneca, built a tool-calling agent (LangChain, Claude Haiku 4.5 on AWS Bedrock) that recovers when its tools fail (circuit breakers with a 19,213-gene parquet fallback, deterministic Ensembl and HGNC calls) and diagnosed its failures layer by layer with a three-tier, ~65-test evaluation harness, which also validated a Groq-to-Bedrock model migration. Owns data workflows end-to-end in Python and SQL, from merging structured, API and web-scraped data through feature creation, tuning, validation and deployment (Docker, GitHub Actions CI/CD, MLflow, AWS Lambda). Production LLM agent work on an AstraZeneca-affiliated multi-omics research platform.",
    "skills": {
      "Agentic AI & LLM Applications": "Tool calling and failure recovery (LangChain, LangGraph, Google ADK, ReAct agent loops; circuit breakers, fallbacks, deterministic guardrails), multi-provider LLMs (OpenAI, Anthropic Claude on AWS Bedrock, Google Gemini via LiteLLM, open-weight models via Ollama), LLM evaluation (three-tier tests, hallucination-rate analysis), agent memory (persistent storage and retrieval across sessions), RAG pipelines (retrieval, generation, embeddings and the ChromaDB vector database), MCP servers (FastMCP, TypeScript SDK), prompt engineering, AI-assisted development (Claude Code as primary tool, Cursor, OpenAI Codex)",
      "Software Engineering & Integrations": "TypeScript/Node.js, React, Python, JavaScript, FastAPI, Pydantic, RESTful APIs and third-party API integrations, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, SQL, MongoDB and DynamoDB (NoSQL), graph data (networkx), pytest, Git (pull requests, code review), debugging and root-cause analysis",
      "Cloud & Deployment": "AWS (Bedrock, Lambda, ECR, S3, SQS, EC2, IAM, Cognito), GCP (Cloud Run), Docker, Kubernetes (AWS EKS), GitHub Actions CI/CD, serverless deployment"
    },
